From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:52:04 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Plutonium: no telemetry, ads or upsells; update checks
 are opt-in

Usage analytics are stripped: AnalyticsService drops every event instead of
batching it to T3's PostHog ingest, the server no longer reads the Claude
and OpenAI account ids (telemetry/Identify.ts is gone), and clients no
longer send hashes of their T3 Connect account and device. Relay traces to
T3's Axiom dataset are never configured. The welcome wizard and Settings no
longer say usage data is collected.

Removed: the GitHub star prompt, the "Created in T3 Code" line in new
projects' READMEs, the T3 Chat upgrade prompts when tunnels run out, the
desktop download links on the hosted pages, and the ChatGPT plan dialog.

Provider update checks (agent CLI versions and model catalog updates) are
off by default; Hydra asks once on its first launch, and Settings,
Maintenance changes it later.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
